# The sdist is what setuptools puts in by default: the package (its modules
# and package-data), pyproject.toml, README.md and LICENSE. Nothing here adds
# to that; every line takes something out. Put any include line above them:
# MANIFEST.in applies its lines in order, so these must come last to win.

# The default rules also take tests/test*.py, and tests/ is a dev-only tree
# (.gitignore), missing from a clean clone.
prune tests

# User settings, credentials (a .env beside the config or at the root), OAuth
# tokens and runtime logs: never shipped, whatever a line above or a stale
# egg-info SOURCES.txt brings in. Each line warns at build time while it has
# nothing to take out.
exclude configs/config.yaml
global-exclude .env
prune .schwabdev
prune .logs

# The strategy plugins that live only in the private source tree (git leaves
# them out). pyproject.toml keeps them out of the build's defaults; these take
# out what an earlier build's SOURCES.txt lists, for the sdist and for a wheel
# built straight from the tree. They too warn while they have nothing to take
# out, as they do in a clean clone.
prune intraday_tv_schwab_bot/_strategies/microcap_gap_orb
prune intraday_tv_schwab_bot/_strategies/microcap_pm_breakout
